WEBVTT

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:36.370
<i>While we were camping 
out at Hinata's house...</i>

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:41.410
It's so pretty.

00:01:41.410 --> 00:01:42.020
Yeah.

00:01:42.730 --> 00:01:45.750
Would it be even prettier, 
seen from Mount Fuji?

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.950
Mount Fuji, huh?

00:01:50.670 --> 00:01:51.420
Mountain Trail

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.420
Season 2 - New Climb 2

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.670
Season 2 - New Climb 2 
Let's Go See Mount Fuji!

00:01:57.170 --> 00:02:01.720
Han032 - Hannou Station

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.720
<i>Hello?</i>

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:03.880
Is that you, Kaede-san?

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:05.140
<i>Hinata-chan?</i>

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:09.410
<i>Yes?</i>

00:02:09.410 --> 00:02:10.810
Hello, Kokona-chan?

00:02:11.290 --> 00:02:13.440
I have a little something to discuss.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.820
Thank you all very much 
for gathering here today!

00:02:20.570 --> 00:02:23.480
There aren't enough of us 
to be referred to as "all."

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.330
So, what's this about?

00:02:25.510 --> 00:02:27.270
Well, you see...

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:32.460
Aoi-chan's interested in Mt. Fuji?

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:33.240
Yes!

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:35.960
So, I want to set up a surprise for her!

00:02:36.620 --> 00:02:39.960
As a pretense, we'll have her climb 
a seemingly ordinary mountain,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.360
until suddenly...

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.970
...we surprise her with a view of Mt. Fuji!

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.850
That makes sense.

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:47.280
How wonderful!

00:02:47.280 --> 00:02:50.350
Kaede-san, do you know of a good place?

00:02:50.350 --> 00:02:51.230
Let's see...

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:53.770
Mountain Guidebook

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.770
Shall we check in the guidebook?

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:59.360
Mt. Kenashi{left middle, orange box}

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:59.360
Mt. Fuji{bottom middle, purple box}

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:59.360
Mt. Mishoutai {slightly right blue box}

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:59.360
Mt. Mitsutouge{middle top red box}

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:59.360
Mt. Tanzawa{far right, blue box}

00:02:54.690 --> 00:02:59.360
Boxes:
- Difficulty
- Popularity
- Scenery

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:55.880
Region...

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.020
Degree of difficulty...

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:59.360
There are a variety of classifications.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.320
We{I?} need to do our best for Aoi-san.

00:03:03.170 --> 00:03:07.560
Places close to Mt. Fuji are 
Mt. Tanzawa, Minami Alps...

00:03:07.560 --> 00:03:09.620
Oh! This photo is amazing!

00:03:09.910 --> 00:03:11.270
Mt. Kita?

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:13.400
It's full of flowery meadows!

00:03:14.010 --> 00:03:15.510
Lovely!

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.610
The fields of flowers are so pretty!

00:03:18.610 --> 00:03:20.630
<i>Ptarmigan, ptarmigan!</i>

00:03:20.630 --> 00:03:23.190
Hello, Mister Ptarmigan!

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.860
Oh, so wonderful...

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:29.140
Mt. Kita!

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:34.110
Kokona-chan, did you find a good place?

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.810
Mt. Kita... would be nice...

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:37.520
Huh?

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.200
It's the second-highest mountain in Japan.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.200
Mt. Kita - Elevation 3143 meters

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:47.200
With a climb even longer and harder than Mt. Fuji, 
this mountain is suited for more advanced climbers.

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:51.910
We can't do that one right away.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:55.010
Why not pick a mountain 
for intermediate climbers?

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:58.590
Aren't there other suitable mountains?

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.440
A mountain from which you 
can see Mt. Fuji, right?

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.840
Let me think... They all seem the same...

00:04:05.030 --> 00:04:06.350
Yeah, no kidding!

00:04:06.350 --> 00:04:08.600
There are way too many similar mountains!

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:10.710
You're right about that.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:12.600
Mountains in Japan...

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.670
even just near Mt. Fuji,

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:21.740
Mt. Fuji

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.960
there's the Tanzawa Mountain Range,

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:21.740
Tanzawa
Mtn. Range

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.190
the Chichibu Mountain District,

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:21.740
Chichibu 
Mtn. District

00:04:17.150 --> 00:04:21.740
Yatsugatake

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:19.100
Yatsugatake, and others...

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:21.740
Misaka
Mtn. District

00:04:19.100 --> 00:04:21.740
There are a lot of mountains 
packed together like this.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:24.040
This is tough.

00:04:24.040 --> 00:04:25.610
It sure is...

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:26.240
Okay!

00:04:27.850 --> 00:04:29.910
We'll pick the mountain 
on the page it opens to!

00:04:29.910 --> 00:04:31.710
Huh? That's sloppy!

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:33.750
You've got to go with gusto sometimes!

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:38.590
Mt. Mitsutouge 
(Yamanashi Prefecture)

00:04:37.130 --> 00:04:38.590
Mitsutouge...

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:40.990
Mt. Mitsutouge.

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:43.840
Mt. Mitsutouge

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:43.840
Elevation, 1786 meters.

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:50.850
Near Mt. Fuji, which is viewable to the 
south, and the Southern Alps to the west.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:59.260
Directly below the summit is a sheer 
cliff{see 'byoubuiwa' translated as 'sheer cliff', literally means 'folding-screen rock' if broken into parts} that is also a climbing spot.

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:04.380
A great view of Mt. Fuji, and 
not too far away? It's perfect!

00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:05.360
Yes!

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:10.210
So then, the mountain we'll use to 
surprise Aoi will be Mitsutouge!

00:05:10.210 --> 00:05:13.560
Don't tell her where we're 
going until we get there!

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.790
Since it's a surprise!

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:16.170
Certainly!

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:19.540
I haven't been to Mitsutouge before, 
so I'm looking forward to it!

00:05:19.820 --> 00:05:22.500
I'll contact Aoi!

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.300
Good work, everyone!

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.970
Good work!

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:34.060
Isn't that...

00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:38.060
It's Mt. Fuji!

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:41.100
Wow! You can even see it from Hannou!

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.270
I never knew that...

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.990
Hinata

00:05:45.030 --> 00:05:46.990
A call from Hinata?

00:05:48.010 --> 00:05:49.250
Hello!

00:05:49.250 --> 00:05:50.500
<i>Uh, Aoi?!</i>

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.370
Hinata! From Hannou you can see Mt. Fu—

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:54.610
<i>We've picked the next mountain to climb!</i>

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.800
That's sudden. Which one?

00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:58.750
<i>It's a secret!</i>

00:05:58.890 --> 00:05:59.910
"A secret"...

00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:03.230
<i>We're meeting next Sunday 6 AM
 at Higashi Hannou station!</i>

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.460
That's so early!

00:06:04.820 --> 00:06:07.360
At <i>Higashi</i> Hannou, not Hannou!

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:07.930
Later!

00:06:11.110 --> 00:06:12.710
It's a secret...

00:06:12.710 --> 00:06:15.440
Where could they be taking me?

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:16.930
Well, that's fine.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.560
I'll just look forward to it.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.890
Towel...

00:06:24.890 --> 00:06:26.500
Change of clothes...

00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:31.530
I don't know what kind of mountain it'll be, 
but these seem like things I should bring.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.490
From Mitsutouge Station, 
take the mountain path...

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.960
Please give her a lovely view of Mt. Fuji!

00:06:45.800 --> 00:06:49.030
And good weather tomorrow...

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:52.930
Good morning!

00:06:53.080 --> 00:06:54.170
Good morning!

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:54.910
'Morning!

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:56.140
Good morning, everyone!

00:06:56.390 --> 00:06:57.860
So, where are we going?

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.290
That's still secret!

00:07:00.790 --> 00:07:02.220
Well, shall we?{literally 'let's go', but then she says it in English}

00:07:02.220 --> 00:07:04.240
Let's go!

00:07:08.070 --> 00:07:11.160
First, we get to Hachiouji 
and change trains there.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.690
Again, where are we going?

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:13.570
Top secret!

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:16.330
Next Stop - Ohtsuke

00:07:14.710 --> 00:07:16.330
Next up, Ohtsuke!

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:18.190
Say, where are we going?!

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:19.700
I told you, it's a secret!

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:20.900
Kokona-chan!

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:21.830
It's a secret.

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:27.800
World Heritage

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:24.610
Tell me!

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:25.710
No way!

00:07:25.710 --> 00:07:26.890
Kaede-san!

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:27.800
It's a secret!

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:30.010
Employees Only{Crew Room? Driver Room?}

00:07:29.510 --> 00:07:31.880
This part will take about thirty minutes.

00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:33.010
You can nap for a—

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:34.680
That was quick!

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.890
Where are we going...

00:07:37.290 --> 00:07:39.470
Shouldn't we just let her sleep?

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.360
<i>...Mitsutouge, Kotobuki...</i>

00:07:40.360 --> 00:07:42.800
<i>...Yoshiike Hot Springs, Shimoyoshida...</i>

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:44.650
<i>...Gekkouji, Mt. Fuji...</i>

00:07:44.650 --> 00:07:45.930
<i>...Fujikyu Highlands...</i>

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:45.930
Uh-oh...

00:07:45.410 --> 00:07:45.930
See?

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.400
<i>...final stop, Lake Kawaguchi.</i>

00:07:45.930 --> 00:07:48.400
They clearly say "Mt. Fuji."

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:53.190
You can see Mt. Fuji very well from here.

00:07:55.280 --> 00:07:58.870
For Mt. Mitsutouge, it'd be easiest 
to get off at Lake Kawaguchi,

00:07:58.870 --> 00:08:02.080
then climb via the Mt. Kachi-Kachi Ropeway.{'Kachi-Kachi Yama' is an old folktale taking its name from Mt. Kachi-Kachi (sound of fire crackling)}

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:06.880
Summit{upper right}

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:10.460
Lake 
Kawaguchi{far left}

00:08:02.700 --> 00:08:05.750
But if we did that, Mt. Fuji 
would be visible from the start.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:10.460
Kawaguchi
Station{middle left}

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:10.460
So even though it's a bit tougher, I decided 
we should climb from Mitsutouge Station.

00:08:06.330 --> 00:08:10.460
Mitsutouge
Station{lower right}

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:10.460
Mt. Fuji{lower left}

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:15.220
Besides, I think going the harder way would 
make the sight of Mt. Fuji even more moving!

00:08:15.590 --> 00:08:16.540
Got it.

00:08:16.940 --> 00:08:21.600
The view of Mt. Fuji from the sheer cliff on 
the way up is supposed to be really pretty,

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:26.100
so that's where we'll give 
Aoi the nice big surprise!

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.360
Mitsutouge

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:34.360
Kotobuki                          Higashikatsura

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.870
Mitsutouge?

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.970
From here it's a thirty-minute 
walk to the mountain path.

00:08:41.350 --> 00:08:45.100
But why did you have to keep that a secret?

00:08:50.630 --> 00:08:52.760
I was really, really scared!

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.660
But when I looked behind me...

00:08:54.660 --> 00:08:55.710
Hinata-san!

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.680
What is it? Something wrong?

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:01.640
It's a UFO!

00:09:02.600 --> 00:09:03.980
Where?! Where?!

00:09:04.320 --> 00:09:06.020
This way!

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:08.520
Oops, it looks like I was mistaken...

00:09:09.910 --> 00:09:11.960
Good job, Kokona-chan!

00:09:11.960 --> 00:09:13.780
I sense trouble ahead...

00:09:13.780 --> 00:09:16.280
Practice Fire Prevention

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:20.500
This way kinda seems more 
like an ordinary road.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:22.950
True, it's not much like a mountain path.

00:09:23.320 --> 00:09:26.460
But once we get on the mountain path, 
we'll be at the summit in no time!

00:09:27.690 --> 00:09:29.730
That's the summit, see?

00:09:29.730 --> 00:09:31.540
Where the antennas are.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:33.840
So that's where...

00:09:34.960 --> 00:09:36.880
This says, "Mitsutouge Mountain Path."

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:45.890
Lord Buddha 
Have Mercy

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:45.890
Mitsutouge Mountain Path

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:41.730
There's a prayer to Buddha 
here too, though...

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:44.480
It's praying for us to have a safe climb!

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:45.890
Okay, let's get going!

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:57.360
Yama... how do you read this?

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.840
It reads, 
"Yamazumi Shrine"!

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:01.870
Yamazumi Shrine

00:10:02.770 --> 00:10:06.450
May we return in good 
health without incident.

00:10:14.860 --> 00:10:16.090
What's that?

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:20.680
Oh, they're public toilets...

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:20.680
Public Toilets

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:30.470
It's a waterfall!

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:32.560
It's called Shinrei Falls!

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:35.530
Ghost

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:34.940
Shinrei, as in <i>ghosts</i>?!

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:39.460
Not "ghosts!" Here Shinrei 
means "Bell of the Gods."

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:41.200
Shinrei Falls

00:10:39.880 --> 00:10:41.200
Oh, so that's all.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:56.750
You are Here

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:56.750
Mountain Path 
to the Left

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:56.750
Mitsutouge Mountain Path

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:56.750
Daruma Rock

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:02.700
It suddenly feels like a real mountain path.

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.200
It really does.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:05.930
Will we be all right?

00:11:06.760 --> 00:11:08.430
Are you ready?

00:11:08.840 --> 00:11:11.900
It'll probably be tough from here on up!

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:18.650
<i>Mt. Mitsutouge...</i>

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.500
<i>Just what sort of mountain is it?</i>

00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:24.620
<i>I'm a little worried, honestly...</i>

00:11:27.860 --> 00:11:31.930
<i>But, since Hinata was making 
such a big deal about it,</i>

00:11:31.930 --> 00:11:36.040
<i>there must be something amazing up ahead!</i>

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:45.350
<i>I just have to walk,</i>

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.250
<i>one step after another,</i>

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:49.330
<i>towards a lovely scene...</i>

00:11:49.720 --> 00:11:53.020
Fuji-Hakone-Izu National Park
Mitsutouge
Elevation 1786 M

00:11:57.620 --> 00:11:59.310
To Be Continued!
